Important variable in Module : _ _name_ _
--------------------------------------------
__name__ is a special Python variable that tells whether a file is executed
directly or imported as a module.

items.py
---------
def itemInfo(name):
    print("Items")
gst=6.8
ball=10
bat=100
print(__name__)

Output
------
__main__    #Use your code not import

stocks.py
---------
from items import ball , bat, itemInfo
print(ball)
itemInfo('ball')

Output
-----
items ----Use items module
10
Items




